1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E04 =- Carol's.Article =- Subripped by zerox

2
00:00:39,130 --> 00:00:41,420
麦克，叫妹妹下来吃饭
Mike, would you get your sister, please?

3
00:00:42,380 --> 00:00:44,120
次货，吃饭!
Yo, Fido, dinner!

4
00:00:45,620 --> 00:00:47,920
水龙头，我来了!
I'll be right down, Fire Hydrant!

5
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:53,000
告诉妈妈我要写完这一段
Tell Mom I'm just gonna finish this paragraph!

6
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:55,940
-妈妈，那个次货说要写完那段话 -谢谢，听见了
- Mom, Fido's gonna finish her paragraph. - Thank you, I heard.

7
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:58,200
水龙头，老实说.
And frankly, Fire Hydrant...

8
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:01,980
称呼妹妹为“次货”一点也不好玩
I don't think it's funny or appropriate for you to call your sister Fido.

9
00:01:02,840 --> 00:01:04,480
对，那是男孩的绰号
You're right. It's a boy's name.

10
00:01:05,140 --> 00:01:06,860
还在写那篇文章？
Is she still working on that article?

11
00:01:07,289 --> 00:01:11,568
她很看重这次的学校报社征稿
Well, she's taking this tryout for the school paper very seriously.

12
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:14,900
爸爸，我们说的是<维特曼时报>.
Come on, Dad, this is the Wait Whitman Chronicle here...

13
00:01:14,900 --> 00:01:16,440
这是“世界有名”的报纸
one of the world's great papers.

14
00:01:17,320 --> 00:01:19,620
名字可是响当当的
It's right up there with Charmin and Nice'n Soft.

15
00:01:20,536 --> 00:01:23,380
麦克，这事对凯罗来说很重要
Mike, this is very important to Carol.

16
00:01:23,380 --> 00:01:25,660
挖苦的话要减少到极点
Try to keep your snide comments to a minimum.

17
00:01:26,360 --> 00:01:27,920
怎样？减少到3句？4句？
So, like, what? Three or four?

18
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:33,015
宝贝，这样太辛苦了
You're working awfully hard, sweetheart.

19
00:01:33,015 --> 00:01:35,223
我要尽量写好
Yeah, well, I just want to get it right.

20
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:38,480
要写出质量最好的稿子
You know, so it's, like, the best article they've ever gotten.

21
00:01:38,888 --> 00:01:41,357
很难打败上周的报道：
Pretty tough to beat last weeks scoop:

22
00:01:41,390 --> 00:01:44,668
<贩卖机上巧克力大战泡泡糖>
"Granola bars replace gummy bears in snack machine."

23
00:01:45,140 --> 00:01:46,060
这算一句
That's one.

24
00:01:47,040 --> 00:01:47,840
一句什么？
One what?

25
00:01:48,197 --> 00:01:52,544
妈妈说吃饭时不能超过4句挖苦
Snide comments. Mom says Mike can make three more at you during dinner.

26
00:01:53,720 --> 00:01:57,340
刚才应该是最后一句了，对不对？
I think probably that was the last one. Right, Mike?

27
00:01:58,400 --> 00:02:00,660
是的，爸爸
Why, yes, Father, I believe it was.

28
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:04,280
明天就见分晓
Anyway, tomorrow's the moment of truth.

29
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:08,860
明天西蒙老师会阅读所有文章 并决定聘请谁
Tomorrow Mr. Simmons reads all the articles and decides who gets the job.

30
00:02:09,160 --> 00:02:11,120
不是西蒙老师吧？
Oh, no, not Simmons.

31
00:02:11,480 --> 00:02:12,500
西蒙老师是谁？
Why? Who's Simmons?

32
00:02:13,120 --> 00:02:16,820
少写了一个双引号就把学生关起来那个
That's the teacher who locked a kid in a closet for not closing a quote.

33
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,600
宝贝，用不着担心
Well, honey, I don't think you have anything to worry about.

34
00:02:20,600 --> 00:02:22,960
只要尽了力，他肯定会欣赏
Just do the best you can, and I'm sure he'll be impressed.

35
00:02:23,580 --> 00:02:28,300
太兴奋了，印刷机的轰隆声
This is so exciting! The roar of the mighty presses.

36
00:02:28,800 --> 00:02:31,100
我的血液充满了墨水
Ink coursing through my veins.

37
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:33,340
也许胜任，也许不能
Maybe I've got what it takes, maybe I don"t...

38
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:37,620
但不全力以赴的话是不会知道的
but I'll never find out if I don't leap into the darkness and give it my all!

39
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:41,700
她继续下去的话我会吐的
If she sings I Gotta Be Me, I swear I'll throw up.

40
00:02:43,360 --> 00:02:44,200
第2句
That's two.

41
00:02:46,780 --> 00:02:47,300
妈妈.
Mom...

42
00:02:47,300 --> 00:02:50,760
今晚能否批阅一下，说说看法
do you think you could read my article tonight and tell me what you think?

43
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:52,840
宝贝，我非常乐意
Why, I'd be happy to, honey.

44
00:02:53,320 --> 00:02:54,220
实话实说？
You'll be honest?

45
00:02:55,200 --> 00:02:56,240
铁面无私
Savagely honest.

46
00:02:56,880 --> 00:03:00,320
也许是我多虑了
I know. I'm probably just worrying for nothing, but...

47
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:04,480
你试过这样全心全意 追求一样东西没有？
have you ever wanted something so much, you could feel it with your entire body?

48
00:03:05,500 --> 00:03:07,000
你不说我还真不知道.
Well, now that you mention it....

49
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:12,920
好吧，我押20块
Yeah, Jerry. Yeah, put me in for $20.

50
00:03:14,260 --> 00:03:15,720
对，我当然有20块
Yeah, of course I have it.

51
00:03:15,985 --> 00:03:20,661
连20块也没有，这不是人渣是什么？
Look, only a scuzzball wouldn't have $20. Yeah, okay. Bye.

52
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:22,220
本，借我20块
Hey, Ben, give me $20.

53
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:23,600
没门
No way.

54
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:27,340
本，本来不想告诉你.
Ben, we didn't want you to know this...

55
00:03:27,340 --> 00:03:31,140
妈妈需要做手术
but, well, Mom needs an operation.

56
00:03:31,333 --> 00:03:33,939
麦克，这个谎话水平也太没水准了
That's low, Mike, even for you.

57
00:03:34,300 --> 00:03:38,680
好吧，杰里在赛马场
Okay, okay, okay. Look, Jerry Dellish is over at Off-Track Betting...

58
00:03:39,040 --> 00:03:41,120
他有第4场“极度难喝”的内幕消息
and hes got a hot tip on Pesky Persky in the fourth.

59
00:03:41,600 --> 00:03:42,760
“极度难喝”是马名？
Is that a horse?

60
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:46,120
当然是马，难道是啤酒？
No, it's an imported beer. Of course it's a horse.

61
00:03:46,360 --> 00:03:49,040
我是给你机会赢100块
Ben, look, I'm giving you the opportunity to make $100.

62
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:54,480
听起来不错
That sounds pretty good.

63
00:03:54,760 --> 00:03:56,058
当然不错
Of course it sounds pretty good...

64
00:03:56,058 --> 00:03:59,494
别一副被我强暴的表情
and you're acting like I'm trying to put one over on you or something.

65
00:03:59,520 --> 00:04:00,500
对不起
I'm sorry.

66
00:04:01,220 --> 00:04:03,140
算了吧，你干不干？
Look, forget it. But you'll do it?

67
00:04:03,580 --> 00:04:05,600
当然了，赢了大家分钱
Sure, and well split the profits.

68
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:06,840
好的
All right, Ben.

69
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:09,060
-我70，你30 -什么？
- 70-30, mine. - What?

70
00:04:10,020 --> 00:04:11,380
不要就算了
Take it or leave it.

71
00:04:11,880 --> 00:04:13,520
好吧，好吧.
Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

72
00:04:13,840 --> 00:04:16,740
合作愉快，麦克
It's a pleasure doing business with you, Mike.

73
00:04:20,120 --> 00:04:21,970
这孩子非池中物
That kids gonna be good.

74
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:29,360
凯罗的文章不至于这样吧？
Carol's paper can't be that bad.

75
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:32,940
她写的是挖蚌的人
She wrote about guys who dig for clams.

76
00:04:34,060 --> 00:04:35,320
有什么不好？
Well, what's wrong with that?

77
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:38,620
题目是<我挖故我在>
She called it, "l Clam, Therefore I Am."

78
00:04:39,501 --> 00:04:40,669
她还在挖？
Did she now?

79
00:04:41,160 --> 00:04:42,260
听听看.
Listen to this:

80
00:04:43,840 --> 00:04:47,900
“日暮苍穹曜石峡..”
"Night obduces the isthmus neath its obsidian mantle.

81
00:04:48,360 --> 00:04:52,020
“蛤蜊张壳海水呷”
"The mollusks imbibe one last sip twixt their vaI'ves...

82
00:04:52,960 --> 00:04:56,020
“黏液仍在颊”
"and expel the days muculence."

83
00:04:56,660 --> 00:04:58,140
是夸张了一点
She could be pushing a little.

84
00:04:58,580 --> 00:05:00,080
杰森，你自己看
Jason, read this.

85
00:05:01,620 --> 00:05:05,400
“挖蚌人像六指琴魔，七上八下..”
"With dexterous manipulation of his digits, the master clammer...

86
00:05:06,060 --> 00:05:08,740
“把润滑的软体动物..”
"extricates the muculent mollusk...

87
00:05:08,898 --> 00:05:11,573
“从青金石下揪了出来”
"from its lapideous menage."

88
00:05:13,860 --> 00:05:15,420
这样看吧.
Well, look at it this way.

89
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:17,820
我们的女儿知道什么是软体动物
We have a daughter who knows what muculence is.

90
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:20,480
有多少人知道什么是软体动物？
How many people know what muculence is?

91
00:05:20,860 --> 00:05:24,700
没有人知道，这也是问题所在
Nobody knows what muculence is, and that's the problem.

92
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:29,380
报刊文章应该写得一目了然
Newspaper writing needs to be clear, accessible.

93
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:35,420
杰森，我该怎么说？ 她需要我实话实说
Jason, what am I gonna tell her? She asked for my honest opinion.

94
00:05:35,720 --> 00:05:37,820
哪个孩子能接受实话？
No kid want's your honest opinion.

95
00:05:38,440 --> 00:05:40,520
她们需要无条件的支持
They want unconditional approval.

96
00:05:41,020 --> 00:05:42,380
要是不赞成呢？
And what if you don't approve?

97
00:05:43,180 --> 00:05:46,740
那样就会进退两难，像现在这样
Then you have a significant dilemma, much like the one you're in now.

98
00:05:47,069 --> 00:05:49,505
谢谢你，西弗医生
Thank you, Dr. Seaver.

99
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:52,420
拜托帮帮忙
Come on, Jason. Help me out here.

100
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:56,200
这次就当作学习的机会
Well, look, we want this to be a learning experience for her.

101
00:05:56,200 --> 00:05:58,100
-继续 -学习是基于.
- Go on. - And all learning is based...

102
00:05:58,100 --> 00:06:00,060
-我们正面的鼓励 -继续
- on positive reinforcement. - More.

103
00:06:00,480 --> 00:06:03,360
有如训练鸽子，你要赏它一颗小球
See, if you want a pigeon to perform, you reward it with a pellet.

104
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:04,580
什么意思？
What are you saying?

105
00:06:04,660 --> 00:06:07,280
我说我们应该养鸽子，鸽子比人好养
I'm saying we should have had pigeons. They're easier to raise.

106
00:06:08,060 --> 00:06:09,440
杰森，别逗了
Jason, come on.

107
00:06:09,760 --> 00:06:14,300
一开始指出文章的长处.
You just start off by pointing out the strengths of the article...

108
00:06:14,360 --> 00:06:17,280
接着你示范如何改进
and then you show her how the article could be improved.

109
00:06:17,540 --> 00:06:18,420
说得对
You're right.

110
00:06:20,020 --> 00:06:21,800
-突出优点 -对
- Accentuate the positive. - Yes.

111
00:06:21,800 --> 00:06:24,240
要婉转，同情，热情
Be gentle and nurturing and supportive.

112
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:26,440
若不行的话.
Then, if that doesn't work...

113
00:06:26,520 --> 00:06:29,680
把她绑起来，烧掉她的名贵球鞋
you simply tie her to the bed and set her Reeboks on fire.

114
00:06:35,360 --> 00:06:35,920
凯罗？
Carol?

115
00:06:37,740 --> 00:06:38,620
进来
Come in.

116
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:50,780
这么晚你一定是累了，明天再谈
Well, it's late. You must be tired. We can talk about this in the morning.

117
00:06:50,940 --> 00:06:52,920
不，我在等着你呢
No, no, I've been waiting for you.

118
00:06:54,536 --> 00:06:59,441
我把文章又看了一遍 现在能够更客观了
I've read the article again, and I think I can be more objective now.

119
00:06:59,720 --> 00:07:04,520
把文章搁下来一段时间，这样做很好
Well, that's a good thing to do. Put it away for a while, get some distance.

120
00:07:04,740 --> 00:07:08,240
-接着就会发现之前完美的地方.. -我知道，已经改了
- Often what you thought was perfect-- - I know, I know. I already changed it.

121
00:07:08,860 --> 00:07:09,740
是吗？
You did?

122
00:07:10,240 --> 00:07:10,760
是的
Yeah.

123
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:16,880
软体动物这词出现了两次，太糟糕了
The two "muculences" in the same sentence. Terrible.

124
00:07:17,426 --> 00:07:21,237
我把第二个改成“贝壳类动物”
I made the second one "pituitousness."

125
00:07:23,320 --> 00:07:23,920
噢!
Oh!

126
00:07:24,620 --> 00:07:26,800
骄傲吧？说实话
Are you proud of me, Mom? The truth.

127
00:07:28,080 --> 00:07:31,080
不错，我为你而骄傲
Of course. Honey, I am always proud of you.

128
00:07:31,380 --> 00:07:32,320
我能成为记者？
You think I'll make the paper?

129
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:37,960
显然你有潜力
Well, it's obvious you have potential.

130
00:07:39,160 --> 00:07:41,760
能写出这种文章的人.
Very few people could write like...

131
00:07:42,720 --> 00:07:42,820
少之又少
this.

132
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:47,620
那我就不用做任何改动了
So you don't think I should change anything. Mom, this is great.

133
00:07:49,660 --> 00:07:50,320
这个.
Well...

134
00:07:50,320 --> 00:07:52,700
我要说的是.
what I'm saying is...

135
00:07:53,680 --> 00:07:58,020
这篇文章你花了很长的时间
Carol, it's clear that you put a lot of time into this article.

136
00:07:58,634 --> 00:08:01,605
构思很好
It's well thought out.

137
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:04,020
打字清晰
It's well typed.

138
00:08:06,440 --> 00:08:08,980
还有这些边框格式很好
And I just love these margins.

139
00:08:09,111 --> 00:08:10,613
但是呢？
But?

140
00:08:11,060 --> 00:08:13,415
也不用接一个“但是”
Well, it's not so much a "but"....

141
00:08:13,415 --> 00:08:15,452
听起来你要说“但是”
It sounds just like a "but."

142
00:08:15,600 --> 00:08:18,380
我要说的是.
Well, what I'm trying to say is--

143
00:08:18,380 --> 00:08:20,000
说出“但是”什么吧
Cut to the "but, " Mom.

144
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,060
但是.
But...

145
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:27,140
这不适合报章
it's just not newspaper writing, honey.

146
00:08:30,320 --> 00:08:33,400
每个领域都有规矩
Look, in any field there are rules.

147
00:08:33,820 --> 00:08:35,180
你学学就懂的了
You just have to learn them.

148
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:39,860
报刊文章应该简单明了，开门见山
Newspaper writing has to be more simple, straightforward.

149
00:08:41,276 --> 00:08:44,622
你认为我的文章是垃圾
So you think my articles garbage.

150
00:08:49,320 --> 00:08:49,920
宝贝.
Sweetheart...

151
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:53,160
若是交给西蒙老师.
if I let you turn this in to Mr. Simmons...

152
00:08:54,240 --> 00:08:56,340
他也会如是说，只会更严厉
He'd tell you the same things, only meaner.

153
00:09:04,820 --> 00:09:06,440
<新闻学入门>
"Introduction to Journalism."

154
00:09:07,420 --> 00:09:10,940
这对我很有帮助，相信对你也是
I found it very helpful, and I'm sure you will, too.

155
00:09:12,360 --> 00:09:12,860
是的
Yeah.

156
00:09:19,948 --> 00:09:21,382
没事吧？
Are you okay?

157
00:09:21,400 --> 00:09:22,420
我没事
Yeah, I'm fine.

158
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:29,200
真的？
Really?

159
00:09:29,820 --> 00:09:31,720
真的，谢谢你的意见
Yeah, really. Thanks for your advice.

160
00:09:32,161 --> 00:09:32,540
很好
Good.

161
00:09:32,540 --> 00:09:35,980
宝贝，晚安
Good night, pumpkin.

162
00:09:44,273 --> 00:09:46,811
<新闻学入门>
"Introduction to Journalism."

163
00:09:51,313 --> 00:09:54,160
杰里说第8场应该买浪涛那匹马
I know. Jerry says we bet on Undulate in the eighth.

164
00:09:54,160 --> 00:09:55,960
应该买霸王那匹
I say we bet on Arbitrary.

165
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,920
-为什么？ -不为什么
- Why? - Why not?

166
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:01,320
本，瞧瞧这些纪录
Ben, look at these times.

167
00:10:01,420 --> 00:10:04,960
等到霸王过终点 恐怕你胸毛都长出来了
I mean, you'll be growing chest hair before Arbitrary finishes this race.

168
00:10:05,140 --> 00:10:06,960
我这次有预感
I just got a hunch about this one.

169
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,420
本，押注不能靠预感
Ben, you cant bet a race on a hunch.

170
00:10:10,332 --> 00:10:15,646
但是霸王最近4场比赛的情形.
Okay, what about that Arbitrary comes out of Secretariat by way of Seabiscuit...

171
00:10:15,680 --> 00:10:18,800
跟<奔腾年代>里描述的故事很像
and Alonzo picked up three purses in his last four turf outings?

172
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:25,520
这个我知道，我们还是相信杰里吧
Hey, I know that, but I say we stick with Jerry.

173
00:10:25,520 --> 00:10:27,580
他到目前为止都很准
I mean, hes been right so far.

174
00:10:27,760 --> 00:10:28,860
我不太放心
I'm not so sure.

175
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:31,700
关系是谁拉过来的？
Ben, who's got the connections?

176
00:10:31,940 --> 00:10:33,000
钱是谁的？
Who's got the money?

177
00:10:33,060 --> 00:10:34,480
我俩谁有体重优势？
Who's got the weight advantage?

178
00:10:34,856 --> 00:10:36,768
买那匹浪涛!
Go, Undulate!

179
00:10:39,340 --> 00:10:40,380
醒醒好吗？
Earth to Maggie.

180
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:44,580
没事吧？
Everything okay?

181
00:10:45,400 --> 00:10:45,960
Oh.

182
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:50,400
凯罗为什么还不下来
Well, I was just wondering why Carol hasn't come down yet.

183
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:54,880
但愿、昨晚我没有太严厉
I hope I wasn't too hard on her last night.

184
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:57,560
你肯定没有…
No, I'm sure you were just....

185
00:10:57,560 --> 00:10:58,720
除非…
Unless....

186
00:10:58,720 --> 00:11:00,080
你真的烧掉她的球鞋？
Did you burn her Reeboks?

187
00:11:01,640 --> 00:11:05,360
妈妈，圣诞节要什么礼物 我有的是钱
What do you want for Christmas, Mom? Cause my middle name is Money.

188
00:11:05,880 --> 00:11:07,360
如果没记错的话
Correct me if I'm wrong...

189
00:11:07,420 --> 00:11:09,980
你是本.汉弗莱.西弗吧？
but I've been living under the assumption your middle name was Humphrey.

190
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:14,429
我讨厌这个名字 我有65块，应该够改名字了
I hate Humphrey, and a kid with $65 can call his own shots.

191
00:11:14,429 --> 00:11:15,664
是吗？
Really?

192
00:11:15,664 --> 00:11:18,867
哪来的65块？
Ben, where did you get $65?

193
00:11:18,867 --> 00:11:20,438
我和麦克.
Well, me and Mike--

194
00:11:20,440 --> 00:11:23,238
是我挣到了钱 你们教导我做人要行善好施
I came into a little money, Mom, and you've always taught me to share...

195
00:11:23,238 --> 00:11:25,310
于是我和弟弟一起分享
so I'm sharing it with my little bro.

196
00:11:26,800 --> 00:11:29,340
麦克，别瞎编了 说实话
And now, just for the heck of it, Mike, the truth.

197
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:32,000
杰里帮我们买马，赢了
Jerry Dellish bet on a horse for us, and we won.

198
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:36,980
麦克，你拿本的钱去赌博？
Mike, you took Ben's money and risked it on a horse?

199
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:40,080
杰里说肯定会赢的
It was a sure thing, Mom. Jerry Dellish said so.

200
00:11:40,560 --> 00:11:42,540
那个花心的杰里？
Jerry "l-swear-she-looked-18" Dellish?

201
00:11:44,460 --> 00:11:45,927
以后不准再赌
There will be no more betting.

202
00:11:45,927 --> 00:11:47,329
-但是我们赢了 -妈妈…
- But, Mom, we won! - Mom--

203
00:11:47,329 --> 00:11:50,140
-杰里… -等等…
- Jerry-- - But wait. But, Mom...

204
00:11:50,500 --> 00:11:53,100
他们运气来了，赢马了…
these guys are hot. They're on a roll. They won.

205
00:11:54,020 --> 00:11:58,660
当然也有不少人在赛马场输钱…
Now I'm sure there are some people who actually lose money at the track...

206
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:03,040
因为他们不认识杰里
but those people don't know Jerry Dellish.

207
00:12:08,500 --> 00:12:11,040
杰森，或许你说得对
Well, maybe you're right, Jason.

208
00:12:11,140 --> 00:12:15,080
孩子们有把握赢钱
These boys do seem to have "winner" written all over them.

209
00:12:15,200 --> 00:12:17,560
那么第8场可以买那匹浪涛了？
So we can let it ride on Undulate in the eighth?

210
00:12:18,300 --> 00:12:22,020
孩子们，站在朋友的角度…
Boys, and I say this to you as a friend...

211
00:12:23,120 --> 00:12:25,060
我说不押就傻了
I think you'd be crazy not to.

212
00:12:25,100 --> 00:12:27,440
-太好了 -我们要赢了
- Yeah, all right! - Were in the money.

213
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:29,600
-谢谢，再见 -要赢钱了
- Thanks a lot. See you later. - Were in the money.

214
00:12:34,876 --> 00:12:36,754
别着急，我的办法可行
Don't worry, this will work.

215
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:37,679
我赌2块
$2 says you're a loser.

216
00:12:37,679 --> 00:12:39,557
-好吧 -奉陪
- You're on. - Okay.

217
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:44,740
凯罗？
Carol?

218
00:12:47,980 --> 00:12:49,700
别担心，她没事
Don't worry, she'll be fine.

219
00:12:50,340 --> 00:12:54,620
西弗家的人，受得起批评
After all, she is a Seaver. She can take criticism. Okay?

220
00:12:59,020 --> 00:13:00,560
凯罗，早上好
Good morning, Carol.

221
00:13:02,880 --> 00:13:05,000
-真漂亮 -谢谢
- You look nice. - Thank you.

222
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:09,420
这毛衣很好看
That's a real cute sweater.

223
00:13:10,700 --> 00:13:11,380
喜欢吗？
You like it?

224
00:13:12,100 --> 00:13:14,660
很喜欢，颜色亲托出你的大眼睛
A lot. It's a good color for you. It brings out your eyes.

225
00:13:14,860 --> 00:13:15,960
不会太鲜艳吗？
It's not too bright?

226
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:18,480
很相称
It's very becoming.

227
00:13:18,900 --> 00:13:21,300
不然我可要找书看了，例如…
You sure? If not, I imagine theres a book I could read...

228
00:13:21,300 --> 00:13:23,260
<穿着入门>
perhaps Introduction to Dressing?

229
00:13:31,540 --> 00:13:33,240
这也叫做事实？
You call these facts?

230
00:13:34,060 --> 00:13:37,500
有多少学生吃过鱼肉后呕吐了？
How many kids threw up from the tuna casserole?

231
00:13:37,973 --> 00:13:41,512
饭堂那边的说法是怎样的？
And where is the cafeterias side of the story?

232
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:43,880
饭堂表示无可奉告
Food Services had no comment.

233
00:13:44,600 --> 00:13:47,100
“饭堂无可奉告”
"Food Services had no comment."

234
00:13:47,840 --> 00:13:49,700
马上回到饭堂采访
You go back down to the cafeteria.

235
00:13:49,840 --> 00:13:53,380
听听做三明治和布丁的人的看法
Somebody in sandwiches or in pudding has an ax to grind.

236
00:13:53,720 --> 00:13:57,440
自己好好想想，再写一份
You find yourself a Deep Throat, and you bring back a story.

237
00:13:58,940 --> 00:13:59,660
下一个
Next.

238
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:07,400
坐下
Sit down.

239
00:14:08,120 --> 00:14:08,960
谢谢
Thank you.

240
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:12,860
凯罗？
Carol, eh?

241
00:14:19,700 --> 00:14:24,520
想当记者？批准
All right, you want the job? You got it.

242
00:14:25,320 --> 00:14:30,380
真的？你喜欢我的文章？ 我花了许多时间在比喻那里
Really? You like my writing? I worked so hard on my metaphors.

243
00:14:30,640 --> 00:14:31,840
你的比喻太臭了
Metaphors stink.

244
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:36,198
-明喻的地方… -明喻也太臭了
- Similes are more-- - Similes stink.

245
00:14:36,198 --> 00:14:38,509
你的文章太臭了
Your writing, it stinks.

246
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:39,880
什么？
What?

247
00:14:40,900 --> 00:14:43,380
不好意思，我忘记在和谁说话了
Excuse me, I forgot who I was talking to.

248
00:14:43,780 --> 00:14:46,660
一股腐臭的味道充斥着这篇文章
It is replete with stinkiosity.

249
00:14:48,280 --> 00:14:52,414
不过至少你没写错字，他们错字百出
But at least you can spell. The others, they cant even spell.

250
00:14:52,414 --> 00:14:56,055
你却写出了没有人懂的词
But you spell words that nobody knows.

251
00:14:56,518 --> 00:14:58,293
软体动物!
Muculence!

252
00:14:58,880 --> 00:15:00,860
究竟什么叫做软体动物？
What in the hell is muculence?

253
00:15:01,623 --> 00:15:03,625
那个…
Well, its....

254
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:06,860
基本上…
It's basically...

255
00:15:06,860 --> 00:15:07,440
就是蚌
slimy glop.

256
00:15:07,800 --> 00:15:10,380
那直接写蚌就好了
Then you call it slimy glop!

257
00:15:10,700 --> 00:15:13,820
大家都知道什么是蚌
People know what slimy glop is.

258
00:15:15,100 --> 00:15:19,500
-可是我认为… -“认为”这词不适合这里
- Yeah, well, I just felt that maybe it was-- - Felt is for pool tables.

259
00:15:21,420 --> 00:15:22,840
周一开始工作
You start Monday.

260
00:15:24,446 --> 00:15:27,051
谢谢，我不要这份工作了
Well, thank you, but I don't think I want the job.

261
00:15:28,900 --> 00:15:30,819
远处拐弯，小姑娘领先
Around the far turn, it's Nice Girl in the lead.

262
00:15:30,819 --> 00:15:32,594
-浪涛，加油! -浪涛，加油!
- Come on, Undulate! - Come on, Undulate!

263
00:15:32,720 --> 00:15:35,700
小姑娘领先修门人6个马位
It's still Nice Girl a full six lengths ahead of Hedge Trimmer...

264
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,700
浪涛远远落后
with Undulate a distant third.

265
00:15:37,920 --> 00:15:41,140
浪涛可能要落下了
Hey, guys, it looks like Undulates gonna be very late.

266
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:45,040
别急，小姑娘前期太用力，后劲不足
Relax. Nice Girl always starts strong. Shell fade.

267
00:15:45,040 --> 00:15:47,060
小姑娘后劲不足
And Nice Girl's starting to fade.

268
00:15:47,500 --> 00:15:48,960
浪涛，加油!
Now, come on, you can do it, Undulate.

269
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:52,900
别着急，它会从外围超越
Don't worry. She'll make her move on the outside, right here.

270
00:15:52,940 --> 00:15:56,060
浪涛从外围赶上
And let's see, moving on the outside, it's Undulate.

271
00:15:56,700 --> 00:15:59,340
瞧它的驰骋!最后冲刺了
Look at her go! And they're moving down the final stretch.

272
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:02,140
齐头并进，小姑娘，浪涛
They're neck and neck. It's Nice Girl, Undulate.

273
00:16:02,400 --> 00:16:03,900
小姑娘，浪涛
Nice Girl, Undulate.

274
00:16:04,080 --> 00:16:06,340
冲线了.
And at the finish, it's...

275
00:16:06,940 --> 00:16:09,040
浪涛险胜
Undulate! By a nose hair.

276
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:12,720
赔率是1赔9
And she'll pay off at nine to one, folks.

277
00:16:12,900 --> 00:16:15,520
-1赔9 -天哪!是450大洋
- Nine to one? - Holy cow! That's $450.

278
00:16:17,499 --> 00:16:20,602
一定是杰里从马场打来 我们怎么办？
All right, that's Jerry calling from OTB. What do we do, Fast Benny?

279
00:16:20,602 --> 00:16:23,138
收下450块还是押到第9场的吞噬者？
We keep the $450 or let it ride on Nail Biter in the ninth?

280
00:16:23,138 --> 00:16:25,440
孩子们，我认为应该激流勇退
You guys, I think you should quit while you're ahead.

281
00:16:25,920 --> 00:16:26,360
杰森!
Jason!

282
00:16:28,620 --> 00:16:32,240
麦姬，450块啊，存进银行 算算利息.
Maggie, it's $450. You put that in a rollover account, with interest the way....

283
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:33,500
拜托
Come on.

284
00:16:33,840 --> 00:16:37,200
我们下次再教育他们吧，好吧
We could teach them this gambling lesson another time, you know. Okay.

285
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,980
孩子们，当运气好时，应该乘胜追击
Boys, I say this is no time to stop. You know, you got it. You got that touch.

286
00:16:45,060 --> 00:16:47,100
好吧，杰里，全部买吞噬者
All right, Jerry, put it all on Nail Biter to win.

287
00:16:50,500 --> 00:16:53,840
凯罗，西蒙老师怎么说了
Hi, Carol. How did it go with Simmons?

288
00:16:54,520 --> 00:16:56,040
很好，他聘用我了
Fine, thank you. I got the job.

289
00:16:56,540 --> 00:16:58,807
真的.
Oh, really? Well....

290
00:16:58,807 --> 00:17:02,551
宝贝，恭喜你，太好了
Well, congratulations, honey. That's wonderful.

291
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:04,946
凯罗当上记者了
Carol got the job on the paper.

292
00:17:04,946 --> 00:17:06,980
作家!作家!
Author, author.

293
00:17:06,980 --> 00:17:08,420
我拒绝了
I turned it down.

294
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:24,780
可以进来吗？
Can I come in?

295
00:17:25,720 --> 00:17:26,060
可以
Sure.

296
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:30,620
在干嘛？
What are you doing?

297
00:17:31,760 --> 00:17:33,000
清理垃圾
Cleaning this garbage out of my way.

298
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:38,960
凯罗，怎么拒绝这次机会了？
Carol, how come you turned the job down?

299
00:17:39,500 --> 00:17:41,780
你不是一心要当记者吗？
I mean, it really seemed like you had your heart set on it.

300
00:17:41,780 --> 00:17:43,218
那时候我还没意识到.
Yeah, well, that was before I realized...

301
00:17:43,218 --> 00:17:45,687
报刊文章不需要创造性
theres nothing really creative about journalism.

302
00:17:45,860 --> 00:17:47,700
只不过是堆砌事实
I mean, all you do is regurgitate facts.

303
00:17:49,658 --> 00:17:52,866
要写作的话，我宁愿、写小说
If I were going to be a writer, I'd rather do a novel.

304
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,160
至少没有人会模仿<白鲸记>
At least people don't train their puppies on Moby-Dick.

305
00:18:00,020 --> 00:18:03,200
凯罗，我知道批评了你.
Carol, I can understand you being angry at me...

306
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,780
你在生我的气
for my criticism of your article.

307
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:08,940
犯不着生气，西蒙老师通过了
Why should I be angry? Simmons gave me the job.

308
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:10,540
我知道
I know.

309
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:16,160
我要说的是.
I know, and I guess what I'm trying to say is....

310
00:18:16,360 --> 00:18:20,740
批评心爱的人是一件很难的事情
Well, honey, it's always tricky giving criticism to someone you love...

311
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,820
也许我的做法不够妥当
and I guess I just didn't do a very good job.

312
00:18:26,140 --> 00:18:28,580
西蒙老师很赞赏你的写法
Obviously, Simmons was very happy with what you did...

313
00:18:28,580 --> 00:18:30,300
我庆幸我错了
and I'm glad that I was wrong.

314
00:18:32,540 --> 00:18:33,000
不是的
No.

315
00:18:36,140 --> 00:18:36,860
什么？
Pardon me?

316
00:18:37,240 --> 00:18:40,680
我说不是的，高兴了吧？ 他的话跟你大致一样，只是更严厉
I said no, okay? Are you happy? He said everything you said, only worse.

317
00:18:45,060 --> 00:18:47,200
他说我的文章.
He said my article was...

318
00:18:48,817 --> 00:18:51,126
“充斥着一股腐臭的气味”
"replete with stinkiosity."

319
00:18:52,860 --> 00:18:54,656
你不是说通过了吗？
But you said that you got the job.

320
00:18:54,656 --> 00:18:59,059
是的，因为其它文章更加臭气熏天
Yeah, that was only cause all the other articles were repleter with stinkiosity.

321
00:19:01,120 --> 00:19:03,660
真遗憾
Honey, I am so sorry.

322
00:19:04,100 --> 00:19:06,920
他说他不知道什么是软体动物
He said he didn't even know what muculence was.

323
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,920
那.
Well, that's....

324
00:19:09,640 --> 00:19:12,200
那是他孤陋寡闻
That's just his stupidity, sweetheart.

325
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,500
大家都认识软体动物
Everybody knows what muculence is.

326
00:19:16,300 --> 00:19:18,780
我永远也不能像你那样写作
I'll never be able to write like you.

327
00:19:19,420 --> 00:19:22,140
等等，不是的
Hold on. Hold on, honey. That's just not true.

328
00:19:22,860 --> 00:19:24,780
你也许会感到有点.
Now maybe you were reaching a little...

329
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:28,320
但是你有天分
but you have great natural ability.

330
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:30,080
你只是安慰我
You're just saying that.

331
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:37,480
你不记得昨天的事了？
Didn't I establish myself last night...

332
00:19:37,480 --> 00:19:39,540
我并不害怕说真话
as someone who isn't afraid to tell the truth?

333
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:42,420
是的
Yeah.

334
00:19:43,700 --> 00:19:46,180
尽管会让一个小孩子心碎
Even if it does mean crushing a little kids ego.

335
00:19:51,646 --> 00:19:54,991
你真的认为我有天分？
Do you really think I might have natural ability?

336
00:19:57,900 --> 00:20:00,400
这是下午从阁楼找到的
I dug this out of the attic this afternoon.

337
00:20:01,020 --> 00:20:04,860
你要看看吧？
And I thought that you might like to take a look at it.

338
00:20:05,960 --> 00:20:08,280
五年前夏令营时我的家信
The letter I wrote from camp five years ago?

339
00:20:09,320 --> 00:20:09,980
念念
Read it.

340
00:20:15,680 --> 00:20:19,080
“亲爱的爸爸妈妈，夏令营很好玩”
"Dear Mom and Dad, camp is fun.

341
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:24,180
“除了观察毒漆藤时 我得了红诊这一点”
"Except for the rash I got when I tried to find out what poison sumac looks like.

342
00:20:24,780 --> 00:20:29,100
“除了大家取笑我是左撇子 长得矮这一点”
"Except for the kids teasing anyone who's small or fat or left-handed.

343
00:20:29,920 --> 00:20:32,080
还有想念你和本宝宝
"Except for missing you and baby Ben.

344
00:20:33,254 --> 00:20:36,167
“甚至有点想念麦克，但别告诉他”
"And even Mike a little, but don't tell him.

345
00:20:36,540 --> 00:20:39,600
“探望我记得带上我的实验设备和薯条”
"Bring my chemistry set and potato chips on visiting day.

346
00:20:40,620 --> 00:20:41,420
“凯罗字”
"Love, Carol."

347
00:20:43,860 --> 00:20:45,000
写得不大好
That's not so good.

348
00:20:47,900 --> 00:20:51,160
我们把实验设备和薯条都带去了
Didn't we bring your chemistry set and your potato chips?

349
00:20:51,780 --> 00:20:52,340
是的
Yeah.

350
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:56,320
那么就是言简意骇
Then you got your point across.

351
00:20:57,400 --> 00:20:57,980
是的
Yeah.

352
00:20:57,980 --> 00:20:58,940
是的
Yeah.

353
00:21:00,000 --> 00:21:01,349
我懂你意思了
Yeah, I see what you're saying.

354
00:21:01,349 --> 00:21:02,360
很好
Good.

355
00:21:02,360 --> 00:21:04,520
不过还能写得更好
But I still think it could have been better.

356
00:21:05,460 --> 00:21:07,320
还能怎么写？
Now, what makes you say that?

357
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:11,300
写上千万别把麦克带来
Well, as I remember, you brought Mike, too.

358
00:21:15,820 --> 00:21:17,560
真是不可思议
And this is unbelievable.

359
00:21:17,740 --> 00:21:21,260
最后的拐弯，吞噬者领先18个马位
Coming around the final turn, it's Nail Biter by 18 lengths.

360
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,740
第二名青蛙远远落后
Running a distant second is Slim's Frog...

361
00:21:24,060 --> 00:21:25,840
还有阿诺之梦在第三位
with Arnold's Dream Date in third position.

362
00:21:25,840 --> 00:21:27,108
-吞噬者! -吞噬者!
- Nail Biter! - Yeah, Nail Biter!

363
00:21:27,108 --> 00:21:30,578
-吞噬者领先20个马位 -吞噬者，冲啊!
- And it's Nail Biter by 20 lengths. - Go, Nail Biter!

364
00:21:30,578 --> 00:21:35,520
吞噬者最后冲刺，领先25个马位
And Nail Biter's at the final pole, and he must be a full 25 lengths ahead.

365
00:21:35,520 --> 00:21:37,051
走路过去也能赢了
That horse could walk in from here.

366
00:21:37,051 --> 00:21:41,159
吞噬者!冲!以后我就衣食无忧了
Go, Nail Biter! I'll never have to work again!

367
00:21:42,220 --> 00:21:45,059
各位且慢，突发意外
Ladies and gentlemen, wait a minute. There's been an accident.

368
00:21:45,059 --> 00:21:49,998
吞噬者坠马倒地
Nail Biter has tripped and gone down. The horse is on the ground.

369
00:21:50,220 --> 00:21:53,320
赛马这么久我还没见过坠马呢
In all my years at the track, I've never seen anything like this.

370
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:54,680
-起来!起来! -起来!
- Get up, get up! - Get up!

371
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:58,200
离终点只剩1尺
A foot from the finish line, maybe two feet...

372
00:21:58,480 --> 00:22:01,680
骑师企图把马拉过终点
and the jockey is trying to drag the horse across the finish.

373
00:22:01,820 --> 00:22:04,720
-快抬起来 -真是壮观!
- Well, pick him up and carry him. - This is amazing.

374
00:22:05,180 --> 00:22:08,483
90斤重的人抓住马腿要拖动一匹马
A 94-pound man trying to drag a racehorse by one leg!

375
00:22:08,483 --> 00:22:09,584
他个子太小了
Hes too small!

376
00:22:09,584 --> 00:22:13,660
-使劲!使劲! -笨蛋，用力!
- Pull him! Pull him! - Come on, you little munchkin, grab him!

377
00:22:13,660 --> 00:22:16,540
小心，外围青蛙追上来了
Look out! Coming up on the outside is Slim's Frog.

378
00:22:16,820 --> 00:22:20,160
第一名是青蛙
And the winner is Slim's Frog!

379
00:22:23,180 --> 00:22:25,740
真是的.
It was just....

380
00:22:25,740 --> 00:22:27,340
你们知道教训了吧
I hope you boys have learned your lesson.

381
00:22:33,408 --> 00:22:35,480
瞧瞧
Look it here.

382
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:39,280
X光照出吞噬者腓骨骨折
"X-rays reveal that Nail Biter suffered a fractured fibula.

383
00:22:39,960 --> 00:22:42,740
教练立刻宣布.
"Trainer Jim Shepherd immediately announced...

384
00:22:42,740 --> 00:22:45,640
这匹纯种马将会变成种马
"that his prize thoroughbred would be put out to stud."

385
00:22:46,321 --> 00:22:48,164
什么是种马？
What's stud?

386
00:22:48,940 --> 00:22:49,500
妈妈
Mom.

387
00:22:51,559 --> 00:22:55,803
有时候公马受了伤.
Well, Ben, sometimes when a boy horse gets hurt...

388
00:22:55,860 --> 00:22:58,920
那么它就要帮许多母马受孕
they use him to get lots and lots of girl horses pregnant.

389
00:22:59,720 --> 00:23:00,860
很好
That's very good.

390
00:23:05,620 --> 00:23:06,260
我的腿!
My leg!

391
00:23:54,499 --> 00:23:55,488
